nodecode-penguin is a rewrite of Crystal32378's Crystal32378/hermes-penguin:

  https://github.com/Crystal32378/hermes-penguin
  commit d63015de74effae451d5286cc080b6a3afddd6ad
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Crystal Chang (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the whole engine, in Common Lisp -- the minute-precision resolution of
a local time to one instant (a time the clocks skipped, a time they read twice,
and the earlier/later choice), the reading of that instant in every zone asked
for, the working-window test with its overnight shift and its equal-hours rule,
the search for the windows where the whole of a meeting fits inside every
member's hours, and the shapes both tools answer. The four tools keep their
names and their arguments (penguin_convert, penguin_overlap, penguin_save_team,
penguin_get_team), the team object keeps its members and windows, and a saved
team keeps the same id rule. One thing changed under the engine: the plugin
carried its own pinned copy of the IANA database, and a cell reads the tz
database this machine already keeps, so the zoneinfo_dir setting names it and
an unreadable one refuses at start. /penguin and the (help :penguin) topic are
additions, not part of the original.

Left out: the Desktop page -- the four-clock planner, the arrival animation,
the control-room artwork, the medal and stamp, the soundtrack and its feature
track, and the /preview route that fed them. A cell has no page of its own, and
the slider's question (does this whole meeting fit?) is answered by
penguin_overlap over the same team. Also left out: Hermes profile state for
saved teams, replaced by one JSON file under the home; and the plugin's
FastAPI routes, which a cell answers as a tool or a slash command.
